THOUGHT: clampToMap dereferences focus, so passing a @Nullable focus from setFocus causes the NullAway error. The simplest safe fix is to handle null at the start of setFocus (e.g., early return) so clampToMap is only called with non-null. I’ll implement an early return when focus is null, which also avoids later dereferences on this.focus.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '138,156s/@Override
  public void setFocus(@Nullable final Point2D focus) {
-    this.focus = this.clampToMap(focus);
-
-    // dunno why but without the factor of 0.01 sometimes everything starts to
+    if (focus == null) {
+      return;
+    }
+
+    this.focus = this.clampToMap(focus);
+
+    // dunno why but without the factor of 0.01 sometimes everything starts to
/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/graphics/Camera.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -m1 "NullAway" new_build_output.log && grep -n "Camera.java" new_build_output.log || true```

